
  The first deploy failed

  ● Write the site files
  ● Set up the database, storage bucket, and email
  ● Commit the site
  ● Store the deploy key in GitHub
  ● Push the site to GitHub
  ■ Run the first deploy
  ○ Connect fieldnotes.example.com
  ○ Sign in to the admin

  What happened     The first deploy failed
                    in GitHub Actions.
  Already done      The completed steps above are kept.
  Left in place     Everything setup created stays,
                    and the next run resumes from it.
  What to do        If the account isn't on Workers Paid,
                    the first deploy fails: check the plan
                    first. Open the run at
                    https://example.test/runs/1 to see
                    what failed. Then run cairn new again.
                    Setup resumes at the first deploy.
